<pdd-reason>Keeps the routes form-agnostic so a second form is a registry entry rather than a branch in the request handler.</pdd-reason>
<pdd-interface>{"type": "module"}</pdd-interface>
<pdd-dependency>i765_schema_Python.prompt</pdd-dependency>

<include>prompts/i765_schema_Python.prompt</include>

Write a small Python module providing the drop-in form registry for the Zuzu
orchestrator, so request handlers never name a specific form.

Requirements:

1. Maintain a registry mapping a form id string to a zero-argument loader that
   returns a `FormSchema`. Seed it with `"I-765"` bound to `get_i765_schema`
   from the schema module.

2. Expose `get_form(form_id: str) -> FormSchema`. Look up case-insensitively and
   tolerate the common spoken and typed variants of the id by normalizing:
   uppercase, and treat `I765` and `I-765` as the same form.

3. Raise `UnknownFormError`, a module-defined exception carrying the requested
   id and the list of known ids, when the form is not registered. The API layer
   turns this into a 404; do not import FastAPI here.

4. Expose `list_forms() -> list[str]` returning the registered ids, and
   `register_form(form_id: str, loader) -> None` so a new form can be added at
   runtime or in a test without editing this module.

5. Resolve loaders lazily and cache the resulting schema per form id, so an
   unused form is never parsed and a used one is parsed once.

6. Type hints throughout. Keep it under roughly sixty lines -- this is a lookup
   table, and any real logic here means it belongs in the schema module.

7. `DEFAULT_FORM_ID` module constant set to `"I-765"`, used by callers that
   need a fallback when the voice agent does not name a form.
